Sec. 15. EXISTING DUTIES ABOLISHED; TRANSFERS PROVIDED.

Subdivision 1.

Duties abolished.

Except as exempted in article 1, section 17, subdivision 7, paragraph (c), duties pertaining to the investigation of fraud, misuse, and other unlawful use of public funds in the Office of the Inspector General in the Department of Education are abolished effective the day after the inspector general appointed under Minnesota Statutes, chapter 15E, certifies in writing to the commissioner of education and the commissioner of management and budget that the inspector general has assumed responsibility for these duties.

Subd. 2.

Inspector general transfers.

When the commissioner of education's duties are abolished under subdivision 1, pursuant to Minnesota Statutes, section 15.039, all active investigations, obligations, court actions, contracts, and records shall transfer from the Department of Education to the inspector general appointed under Minnesota Statutes, chapter 15E, except as provided by the inspector general and as provided in article 1, section 17, subdivision 7, paragraph (c).

EFFECTIVE DATE.

This section is effective July 1, 2026.

